For a long time I never used a newsreader on my own computer, I just
took a telnet or ssh connection to my isp's shell computer and ran the
newsreader there. (Started with rn, then moved over to nn, and when I
changed to my current isp about 10 years ago I changed to gnus.)
Then the isp discontinued the shell service for users and I had to start
running the newsreader on my own machine.

But whenever I want to acces Usenet from somewhere else, I just take the
ssh connection, nowadays to my home, and start the familiar newsreader,
using the same .newsrc and all the settings no matter where I physically
am. Simple as that.

Well, actually I have restricted the ssh server on my computer to only
allow connections from certain ip addresses (like my work computer), so
if I need to connect from somewhere else, I first have to make some
adjustments to my hosts.allow or hosts.deny file, but it doesn't happen
too often.

